  "implemented_contract": {
    "shared_allocator_list": "One caller-supplied AllocatorListElement*& head and one domain. Canonical element contains native vtable/previous/next only (12 bytes Win32); external binding map has no links or private head.",
    "concrete_virtual0": "DirectionalLightPool registers actual vtable 00d62f00/function 00b7ba20/context/invoke. Domain verifies expected current vtable and calls the bound implementation. Unknown or mismatched foreign profiles throw explicit binding failure; traversal reloads current.next after dispatch.",
    "canonical_pool_storage": "Caller-supplied 0x38-byte Win32 owner: element+00, actual critical section+0c, explicit recursion+24, table+28, count+2c, capacity+30, first-free+34. Companion has references only and no automatic native destructor.",
    "slab": "Actual allocation 0x3e44: 32 raw 0x1f0 slots, free indices+3e00, free count+3e40, two untouched tail bytes. Constructor initializes only free stack/count and each live slab ID at slot+1ec.",
    "return_and_compaction": "Return reads actual current +1ec and signed exact slot index. Trim frees empty slabs, swaps last pointer into hole, decrements count, rewrites all 32 moved IDs, retries the same index, then recomputes first available slab; no internal lock or immediate trim on return.",
    "allocation_and_newhandler": "Table allocation 00bf55be jumps to 00bf681b; table free 00bf6989 jumps to 00bf65ac. Reuse actual singleton_lifetime_allocate/free and its CRT new-handler loop; unused table entries and raw slot preimages are not zeroed.",
    "allocation_failure": "No allocation-path catch/finally/RAII. Published first-free index, published grown capacity and held critical-section recursion survive an allocation throw. A new slab allocated before a failed table growth is not appended or automatically freed.",
    "constructor_unwind": "Constructor-only MSVC finally: state0 allocator unlink, state1 critical cleanup then unlink, state2 table free then critical cleanup then unlink. Table/free and unlink leaves preserve stale native words.",
    "destroy": "Install pool vtable; free slabs without light virtual destruction; free table; drain positive explicit recursion through actual LeaveCriticalSection; DeleteCriticalSection; install base vtable 00d7a0c0; unlink same shared element. Do not zero stale table/count/capacity/link words.",
    "static_startup": "Explicit bind_static_directional_light_pool_01090154 required; initialize 00cd8080 constructs that actual owner then registers actual destroy 00ce0eb0 with std::atexit by default or the supplied CRT registration function. Return registration status; no rollback on registration failure. Storage/domain/companion outlive registered callback.",
    "string_pool": "Existing SizedStoragePool remains for names; it is not registered in 00e188b4. Singleton lifetime manager list is also a separate domain."
  },
